{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UzxbmRHG5yfqW3z2cZtHnC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\ttotp\n2\t====\n3\tFrom-scratch, dependency-free implementation of\n4\t[TOTP](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time-based_one-time_password),\n5\tincluding SHA1, for education. TOTP is the most common standard for\n6\tgenerating codes in 'Authenticator' apps.\n7\t\n8\t![Screenshot](screenshot.png)\n9\t\n10\tLive web version: https://sjmulder.nl/totp/\n11\t\n12\tDetails\n13\t-------\n14\tSources:\n15\t - `totp.{c,h}` - the algorithms.\n16\t - `std.{c,h}` - some libc functions for freestanding targets (WASM,\n17\t   GBA).\n18\t - `main.c` - a simple CLI.\n19\t - `test.c` - unit tests.\n20\t - `index.html` - a frondend for the WASM build.\n21\t\n22\tTargets:\n23\t - `totp` - the CLI.\n24\t - `totp{32,64}.exe` - the CLI, for Windows.\n25\t - `totp.wasm` - a WebAssembly build, used by `index.html`.\n26\t\n27\t\n28\tTOTP generators take a seed (the \"shared secret\"), which is usually\n29\tpresented as a QR code or base32-encoded string when setting up the\n30\tauthenticator.\n31\t\n32\tThis implementation generates codes for the current time given a seed,\n33\tbut the CLI nor the WASM web version store seeds for later use.\n34\t\n35\tBuilding\n36\t--------\n37\t - `make` to  build CLI using default C compiler.\n38\t - `make check` to run tests.\n39\t - `make cross` to  build Windows and WASM targets.\n40\t\n41\tFor Windows and WASM, default compilers and flags are specified in\n42\tthe Makefile but can be overridden with make flags or `config.mk`,\n43\twhich is automatically included if it exists.\n44\t\n45\tAuthor\n46\t------\n47\tSijmen Mulder (ik@sjmulder.nl). See LICENSE.md.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a782bdea-3f47-4a74-9323-d3c657455cf7","uuid":"18d5fe16-05fd-45b6-a2a3-d4e08bb292eb","timestamp":"2026-05-29T01:26:07.787Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/harvest-crust-WMpZ0E/project/c_src/README.md","content":"totp\n====\nFrom-scratch, dependency-free implementation of\n[TOTP](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time-based_one-time_password),\nincluding SHA1, for education. TOTP is the most common standard for\ngenerating codes in 'Authenticator' apps.\n\n![Screenshot](screenshot.png)\n\nLive web version: https://sjmulder.nl/totp/\n\nDetails\n-------\nSources:\n - `totp.{c,h}` - the algorithms.\n - `std.{c,h}` - some libc functions for freestanding targets (WASM,\n   GBA).\n - `main.c` - a simple CLI.\n - `test.c` - unit tests.\n - `index.html` - a frondend for the WASM build.\n\nTargets:\n - `totp` - the CLI.\n - `totp{32,64}.exe` - the CLI, for Windows.\n - `totp.wasm` - a WebAssembly build, used by `index.html`.\n\n\nTOTP generators take a seed (the \"shared secret\"), which is usually\npresented as a QR code or base32-encoded string when setting up the\nauthenticator.\n\nThis implementation generates codes for the current time given a seed,\nbut the CLI nor the WASM web version store seeds for later use.\n\nBuilding\n--------\n - `make` to  build CLI using default C compiler.\n - `make check` to run tests.\n - `make cross` to  build Windows and WASM targets.\n\nFor Windows and WASM, default compilers and flags are specified in\nthe Makefile but can be overridden with make flags or `config.mk`,\nwhich is automatically included if it exists.\n\nAuthor\n------\nSijmen Mulder (ik@sjmulder.nl). See LICENSE.md.\n","numLines":48,"startLine":1,"totalLines":48}}}
